From: REIMU A/B <reimu@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] user/channel data: reload when the file was replaced

ipmid writes /var/lib/ipmi/ipmi_user.json to a temporary file and renames
it; netipmid (and ipmid) reload their copy when the file's mtime changed.
jffs2 keeps seconds only: a reader that loaded the file in the same second
as the next write kept the old table. In QEMU on the A/B firmware a user
configured with ipmitool (set name, channel setaccess, enable, password in
a row) was then refused over LAN with "invalid role" until netipmid was
restarted. Tell the versions apart by the inode as well.

---
diff --git a/user_channel/channel_mgmt.cpp b/user_channel/channel_mgmt.cpp
index b8e0b85b..08b36945 100644
--- a/user_channel/channel_mgmt.cpp
+++ b/user_channel/channel_mgmt.cpp
@@ -687,7 +687,14 @@ std::time_t ChannelConfig::getUpdatedFileTime(const std::string& fileName)
         log<level::DEBUG>("Error in getting last updated time stamp");
         return -EIO;
     }
-    return fileStat.st_mtime;
+    // The file is replaced (rename) on every write, and its mtime has 1 s
+    // resolution (jffs2): a process that read it in the same second as
+    // another one rewrote it kept stale data (netipmid refused a user
+    // configured a moment before: "invalid role"). The inode tells them
+    // apart. Only compared for equality.
+    return static_cast<std::time_t>(
+        static_cast<uint32_t>(fileStat.st_mtime) ^
+        (static_cast<uint32_t>(fileStat.st_ino) * 2654435761u));
 }
 
 EChannelAccessMode
